I'm really still inclined to think that blessings from your god should
remain blessings, and the HoE/EoB/SSfA "blessing" is NOT one.

I'm inclined to think the increase of prayer timeout should be
eliminated--it seems odd that faithful servants of their gods should
have to wait longer between prayers.

For those who think long prayer timeouts are essential to later-game
balance, how about this idea:  Make prayer timeout partially dependant
on level.  Say it's 500 turns now (if I have the number wrong, adjust
my other calculations).  Change thi to 450 + 2*(level)^2.  This makes
the timeout:

452     at level 1
500     at level 5
650     at level 10
900     at level 15
1250    at level 20
1700    at level 25
2250    at level 30

This way,
gods are uninclined to answer prayers of POWERFUL characters (which
makes sense), rather than FAITHFUL characters (which makes no sense at
all).

